# SPEC-LINE.md §4 R-D2 (Module D, branch line-version): the deployment-
# ready secrets template for a LINE install -- deploy/setup.sh copies this
# to .env for you (only if .env doesn't already exist). Fill in the three
# values below before starting habit-assistant-line.service; docs/
# DEPLOY-LINE.md walks through getting each one from the LINE Developers
# console.
#
# .env is gitignored -- never commit real values.

# LINE Developers console -> your Messaging API channel -> Basic settings
# tab -> "Channel secret". Used to verify the x-line-signature HMAC on
# every inbound webhook POST (SPEC-LINE.md §2.1/R-A1).
LINE_CHANNEL_SECRET=your-channel-secret-here

# Same console -> Messaging API tab -> "Channel access token" -> Issue
# (long-lived). Used as the Bearer token for outbound Reply/Push API calls.
LINE_CHANNEL_ACCESS_TOKEN=your-long-lived-channel-access-token-here

# Your own LINE userId -- the owner (owner attribution on first startup,
# and every owner-only surface: /audit, /users, admin commands, the digest
# quota warning). Format is "U" + 32 hex chars. Easiest way to get it:
# after the webhook is registered and the service is running, send the bot
# any message from your own LINE account and read the userId out of the
# server log line for that inbound event (or `journalctl -u
# habit-assistant-line -f` while you send it).
LINE_OWNER_USER_ID=U0000000000000000000000000000000
